// Module and package metadata is typed attribute data on the unit's root
// declaration (proposal-packages.md §7), not a new file format: `package`,
// `dependency`, and `toolchain` are built-in inert coordinate schemas that
// share the entity-attribute mechanism, so a manifest is checked gandr data
// hosted inside the source unit. A `dependency` is repeatable (one per
// dependency); `package` and `toolchain` are single-valued.
//
// The manifest's real home is a top-level module declaration. Attribute
// collection is item-generic, so this fixture deliberately uses a `def` to
// isolate the manifest schemas and their typing from module lowering;
// `model/29-modules.gandr` separately exercises the landed module declaration.
// Inert coordinates are hash-neutral: they never perturb the unit's
// content-address (proposal-packages.md §7.4), so editing a coordinate does not
// change the unit's identity — only what resolution later pins does.
//
//@ expect: clean
//@ expect-def: parser_unit
//@ expect-attribute: package
//@ expect-attribute: dependency
//@ expect-attribute: toolchain
@[package(#{ name = "acme/parser", version = "1.4.0" })]
@[dependency(#{ name = "acme/lexer", alias = "lexer", constraint = "^2.1" })]
@[toolchain(#{ gandr = ">=0.9" })]
def parser_unit = ();
